{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "kind": "regCleanProtected",
  "description": "Protected set of the registry cleaner (DECISIONS RG11, RG12, RG15). Anything matching a group is never offered for removal; securityVendors matches are shown as Protected with the removal tool. Names (publisher, display name) only ever add protection, they never make an entry removable (RG5). Validated by Test-IgwtRegCleanProtectedCatalog inside Test-IgwtCatalog.",
  "patternRules": "Wildcards are PowerShell -like patterns, case-insensitive. keyPatterns match HIVE\\path (HKLM\\..., HKCU\\..., HK*\\ for both); the 32-bit view uses the same logical path. pathPatterns start with a drive, a %Variable% or *\\ followed by a folder of at least 4 characters. Name patterns never start with a wildcard. signerPatterns start with CN= or O=. categoryRootsAllowed: category roots (data\\registry\\categories.json) that the group keyPatterns would cover but must not; entries below them are protected by entry-level rules only.",
  "alsoRead": [ "data\\manage\\services.json", "data\\firewall\\apps.json" ],
  "unverified": "Vendor, anti-cheat and hardware names, signer names and the removal tool pages are not first-party Microsoft data (DECISIONS RG28 items 6, 7, 11): used only to protect; re-check the tool pages before a release.",
